        {
          "id": "2c77d64a-fbc6-4865-a212-9f351ce0d39d",
          "name": "Get Upload URL",
          "request": {
            "name": "Get Upload URL",
            "description": {
              "content": "Returns a presigned S3 PUT URL for direct file upload. Lets clients upload files without managing AWS credentials or staging buckets — the server signs a single-use URL bound to a server-generated S3 object key, the client PUTs the file body to that URL, then registers the upload via `POST /v1/sources` with the returned `file_key`.\n\n**Why this exists:** `POST /v1/sources` requires a `file_key` for an object that already exists in our backing storage. Customers without their own staging bucket use this endpoint to obtain an upload URL pointed at the canonical destination directly, eliminating any client-side AWS setup.\n\n**Important — Content-Type binding:** The presigned URL is signed with `Content-Type` baked into the signature. The client **MUST** send a matching `Content-Type` header on the PUT request, otherwise S3 rejects with HTTP 403 (`SignatureDoesNotMatch`). The expected value is returned in the `content_type` field of this response — pass it back as the `Content-Type` header on your PUT.\n\n**Workflow:**\n1. Create a source batch via `POST /v1/source_batches` (returns `source_batch_id`)\n2. Call this endpoint with `name`, `source_type`, `source_batch_id` (returns `upload_url`, `file_key`, `content_type`, `expires_in`)\n3. PUT the file to `upload_url` with `Content-Type: <content_type>` header\n4. Register the source via `POST /v1/sources` with `file_key` from step 2\n5. Poll `GET /v1/sources/{source_id}` until `status: \"success\"`\n6. Reference `source_batch_id` in chat/search requests\n\n**Constraints:**\n- Supported `source_type`: `pdf`, `docx`, `xlsx`, `pptx`, `doc`, `txt`\n- Maximum file size enforced at registration step: 20MB\n- Maximum 10 active sources (status: `processing` or `success`) per source_batch — `failed`/`deleted` sources do not count toward the limit (enforced when generating the URL)\n- URL expires after 10 minutes (`expires_in: 600`)\n- File is validated at registration time (`POST /v1/sources`); a wrong-content upload will be accepted by S3 but rejected when registering",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "sources",
                "upload_url"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": []
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": null,
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"source_type\": \"<string>\",\n  \"source_batch_id\": \"<uuid>\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
